<title>ECUADOR: IMF mission postponed-Ecuador official.</title>
<headline>IMF mission postponed-Ecuador official.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>An International Monetary Fund mission which was due to arrive in Ecuador Thursday has been postponed until at least  the end of July, a government official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The precise date will be decided after the Ecuadorean government has finished revising its budget deficit estimates, Technical Under Secretary for Finance Mauricio Pareja told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;The government wants to an agreement with the Fund which could be a stand-by agreement, but without any disbursement,&quot; said Pareja.</p>
</text>
